WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.1 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Your legal and regulatory map

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Know the legal duties you will carry, and ask the right questions before you launch.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
A legal map lists the legal duties you will carry: where each comes from, who oversees it, when it applies and who is responsible. It helps you ask the right questions before you launch.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Four sources of duties

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:39.352
Your legal form: Association, foundation, charity, company or cooperative: each brings its own registration and governance rules. For example: Registering as a cooperative brings annual member meetings and filing deadlines.

6
00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:49.570
Your activities: Working with children, employing people, handling data, selling food or raising money. For example: The bakery needs food hygiene registration before its first market stall.

7
00:00:49.570 --> 00:01:00.159
Your countries: Each country and region where you work has its own rules. For example: A tutoring service teaching online in two countries maps the rules of both.

8
00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:10.467
Funders and partners: Grant and contract conditions can be legally binding. For example: A start-up grant requires insurance and a safeguarding policy before activities begin.

9
00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:11.467
Why map it now

10
00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:18.252
1. Some duties start before you register; others the day you first hire or sell.

11
00:01:18.252 --> 00:01:24.296
2. Knowing your questions saves time with someone who has a legal background.

12
00:01:24.296 --> 00:01:30.230
3. Funders and partners expect you to know your obligations.

13
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.230
What it feeds

14
00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:36.533
1. Your policy needs assessment and policy register in this module.

15
00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:40.726
2. Your contracts checklist and your risk register.

16
00:01:40.726 --> 00:01:47.030
3. Your calendar: every deadline and frequency, each with an owner.

17
00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.030
What to avoid

18
00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:52.593
Asking legal questions after launch instead of before.

19
00:01:52.593 --> 00:01:57.896
Treating unconfirmed items as settled: mark what has been checked.

20
00:01:57.896 --> 00:02:04.570
Mapping only one country when you plan to work in several.

21
00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:06.970
You build your legal map and a list of open legal questions.

22
00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:10.970
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:15.570
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
